feat(lpa-susceptibility): record the outcome and declare a post hoc rerun

Adds to PREREGISTRATION.md the outcome of the pre-registered run (LS6 job
3602201): verdict INCONCLUSIVE, product of predicted Lp(a) with the
non-lipid score 0.0072 (SE 0.0087).

It also records a flaw in secondary analysis 1: the lipid-region score
contains the LPA locus (three ApoB lead variants there, among them
rs10455872), so the product of Lp(a) with that score (-0.046, P 0.004) had
the same locus on both sides. Declared before it is run: the LPA-region
part of the score is scored separately with the original PLINK2 options
and subtracted, and three models are fitted (original, region removed,
region as its own term), with the reading fixed in advance.

lpa_susceptibility_posthoc.R takes the function definitions of the
pre-registered script without running it; the SLURM wrapper checks every
reused file by md5. Synthetic self-test: LS6 job 3602296, 8 checks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 


